  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PrePhys 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "A research team is testing several new treatment ideas to slow cancer
    progression. Based on your experience caring for patients, you review the preclinical
    data to help the team identify which compounds will move forward into future
    clinical trials.\n\n<b>In this scenario, why is the physician\u2019s input necessary
    before moving forward to trials?</b>"
  explanation: "Physicians help connect what\u2019s learned in the lab to what really
    matters for patients. By helping researchers choose the treatment ideas most
    likely to work for people and fit their needs, physicians help focus efforts
    on the best options before testing begins in patients. This guidance increases
    the chances that treatments moving into clinical trials are safer, more effective,
    and truly meaningful for patients."
  correctAnswer: To determine which treatment ideas align best with disease behavior
    in humans and patient needs
  incorrectAnswer1: To design and conduct laboratory experiments for each treatment
    idea then compare the results
  incorrectAnswer2: To prove which patients will respond to each of the new treatment
    ideas
  incorrectAnswer3: To approve or deny the use of the treatment ideas for immediate
    clinical use
  questionRole: Physician
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: PreClinical
